px] font-medium tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 accent-glow mb-3\">Certificate of Analysis</p><h1 class=\"text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-foreground\">Lot TESA-CA-26F-20 Test Report — Tesamorelin 20mg 20mg</h1><div class=\"mt-4 w-12 h-px bg-brand-300/50 dark:bg-border-strong\"></div><p class=\"mt-5 max-w-2xl text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">This lot of <!-- -->Tesamorelin 20mg<!-- --> (20mg)<!-- --> was independently assayed by <!-- -->Janoshik<!-- --> on 2026-07-23<!-- -->. The figures below are the laboratory’s, published in full rather than summarised. Match the lot code printed on your vial to the code on this page to confirm the vial came from the batch that was tested.</p><div class=\"mt-8 glass rounded-card border border-border/60 p-6\"><dl><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-6 border-b border-border/50 py-2.5 last:border-0\"><dt class=\"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-foreground-muted\">Compound</dt><dd class=\"text-[14px] text-foreground text-right\">Tesamorelin 20mg</dd></div><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-6 border-b border-border/50 py-2.5 last:border-0\"><dt class=\"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-foreground-muted\">Lot</dt><dd class=\"text-[14px] text-foreground text-right\">TESA-CA-26F-20</dd></div><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-6 border-b border-border/50 py-2.5 last:border-0\"><dt class=\"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-foreground-muted\">Strength</dt><dd class=\"text-[14px] text-foreground text-right\">20mg</dd></div><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-6 border-b border-border/50 py-2.5 last:border-0\"><dt class=\"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-foreground-muted\">Purity (HPLC)</dt><dd class=\"text-[14px] text-foreground text-right\">99.375%</dd></div><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-6 border-b border-border/50 py-2.5 last:border-0\"><dt class=\"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-foreground-muted\">Expected content</dt><dd class=\"text-[14px] text-foreground text-right\">20.00 mg</dd></div><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-6 border-b border-border/50 py-2.5 last:border-0\"><dt class=\"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-foreground-muted\">Measured mass</dt><dd class=\"text-[14px] text-foreground text-right\">22.6 mg</dd></div><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-6 border-b border-border/50 py-2.5 last:border-0\"><dt class=\"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-foreground-muted\">Fill accuracy</dt><dd class=\"text-[14px] text-foreground text-right\">113%</dd></div><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-6 border-b border-border/50 py-2.5 last:border-0\"><dt class=\"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-foreground-muted\">Verification lab</dt><dd class=\"text-[14px] text-foreground text-right\">Janoshik</dd></div><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-6 border-b border-border/50 py-2.5 last:border-0\"><dt class=\"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-foreground-muted\">Test date</dt><dd class=\"text-[14px] text-foreground text-right\">2026-07-23</dd></div><div class=\"flex items-baseline justify-between gap-6 border-b border-border/50 py-2.5 last:border-0\"><dt class=\"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-foreground-muted\">Format</dt><dd class=\"text-[14px] text-foreground text-right\">Lyophilized powder</dd></div></dl></div><div class=\"mt-6 max-w-2xl\"><h2 class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-foreground\">Why fill accuracy matters</h2><p class=\"mt-3 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Purity tells you what fraction of the material in the vial is the target compound. It tells you nothing about how much material is in the vial. A vial can assay at 99.8% purity and hold 7 mg against a 10 mg label — the purity figure is accurate and the vial is still short.</p><p class=\"mt-3 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Fill accuracy is the measured mass against the expected content:<!-- --> <!-- -->22.6<!-- --> mg measured against <!-- -->20.00<!-- --> mg expected, or<!-- --> <!-- -->113<!-- -->%. Both numbers are published for every Eppix batch.</p></div><section class=\"mt-10 max-w-2xl\"><h2 class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-foreground\">How to read this certificate</h2><p class=\"mt-3 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Two separate tests sit behind the table above.<!-- --> <strong class=\"font-medium text-foreground\">Identity</strong> is established by mass spectrometry: the measured molecular mass is compared against the mass calculated from the compound’s published sequence or formula, and a match within the instrument’s tolerance is what confirms the material is <!-- -->Tesamorelin 20mg<!-- --> rather than something else.<!-- --> <strong class=\"font-medium text-foreground\">Purity</strong> is established by reversed-phase HPLC and reported as area percent — the fraction of the total chromatographic signal belonging to the main peak.<!-- --> For this lot that figure is 99.375%.</p><p class=\"mt-3 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Area percent is a relative measure, not an absolute one. It says what share of the detected material is the target compound; it says nothing about how much material is in the vial, which is why measured mass is reported alongside it rather than instead of it. A certificate that publishes purity and withholds mass has answered the easier of the two questions.</p><p class=\"mt-3 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">The working threshold for research-grade peptide material is 98% by HPLC area, with 99% and above the range reputable synthesis routinely reaches.<!-- --> At 99.375%, this lot sits inside that range.<!-- --> <!-- -->Nothing on this page is rounded, restated or re-tested in-house: the certificate is <!-- -->Janoshik<!-- -->’s<!-- --> and carries their test date of 2026-07-23<!-- -->.</p><p class=\"mt-3 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">New to reading these?<!-- --> <a class=\"text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/peptide-research/how-to-read-a-certificate-of-analysis\">How to read a certificate of analysis</a> <!-- -->walks through a full report field by field, and<!-- --> <a class=\"text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/peptide-research/purity-vs-fill-accuracy\">purity vs fill accuracy</a> <!-- -->covers why the two numbers have to be read together.</p></section><div class=\"mt-8\"><h2 class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-foreground mb-3\">Full report</h2><div class=\"glass rounded-card border border-border/60 p-3\"><img alt=\"Certificate of Analysis for Tesamorelin 20mg batch TESA-CA-26F-20\" width=\"1000\" height=\"1400\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"1\" class=\"w-full h-auto rounded-lg\" style=\"color:transparent\" sizes=\"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px\" src=\"/reference/1241d5634224e30e3358.webp\"></div></div><div class=\"mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-[14px]\"><a href=\"https://verify.janoshik.com/tests/204104-Tesamorelin_20mg_Eppix_Labs_TXI1PGNFMPKG\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline\">Open the <!-- -->Janoshik<!-- --> report for this batch →</a><a class=\"text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/products/tesamorelin\">Buy <!-- -->Tesamorelin 20mg<!-- --> →</a><a class=\"text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/certificates-of-analysis/tesamorelin\">Full <!-- -->Tesamorelin<!-- --> lot history →</a><a class=\"text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/verify\">Verify another batch →</a><a class=\"text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/certificates-of-analysis\">All batches →</a></div><section class=\"mt-12\"><h2 class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-foreground\">Previous batches of <!-- -->Tesamorelin 20mg</h2><p class=\"mt-2 text-[13px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed max-w-2xl\">Every lot of <!-- -->Tesamorelin 20mg<!-- --> we have published, newest first. Consistency across lots is visible here in a way a single certificate cannot show.</p><ul class=\"mt-4 divide-y divide-border/60 border-y border-border/60\"><li><a class=\"group flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-4 gap-y-1 py-3\" href=\"/certificates-of-analysis/tesa-ca-26f-10\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[12px] tracking-[0.06em] text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 group-hover:underline\">TESA-CA-26F-10</span><span class=\"text-[12px] text-foreground-secondary\">10mg</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[12px] text-foreground-secondary\">98.763<!-- -->% purity</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[12px] text-foreground-secondary\">116.8<!-- -->% fill</span><span class=\"ml-auto font-mono text-[11px] text-foreground-muted\">2026-07-23</span></a></li></ul></section><p class=\"mt-10 text-[12px] text-foreground-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl\">Research use only. Materials supplied by Eppix Labs are intended strictly for in-vitro laboratory research. Not for human or veterinary use, and not for the diagnosis, treatment, cure or prevention of any condition.</p></div></section></div><!--$--><!--/$--></main><div class=\"no-overflow-x\"><footer class=\"glass\"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-16\"><div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 gap-y-12 sm:grid-cols-2 sm:gap-x-10 lg:grid-cols-6 lg:gap-x-10\"><div class=\"sm:col-span-2 lg:col-span-1\"><a class=\"inline-block\" href=\"/\"><img alt=\"Eppix Labs\" width=\"140\" height=\"53\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"1\" class=\"h-12 w-auto opacity-80 dark:hidden\" style=\"color:transparent\" src=\"/reference/542f21d265d782b806de.webp\"><img alt=\"Eppix Labs\" width=\"140\" height=\"53\" decoding=\"as